; Stage 3: semantics, which builds the typed syntax tree. See
; docs/design/semantics.md. The subdirectories say what kind of module each
; is, and `unqualified` keeps every module name flat, so none of them is
; named after its directory:
;
; - model/     the tree and what it is built from: [Nodes], [Ty],
;              [Signature], [Env] and [Intrinsics];
; - passes/    [Assembly] groups files into packages, then [Collect] (passes
;              1 and 2), [Type_decls] (3) and [Verb_signatures] (4);
; - check/     pass 5, [Check], and the parts of it that are not the
;              recursive walk, with [Program] running it over the build;
; - analyses/  [Repeats], [Read_only], [States], [References], [Moves],
;              [Scopes], [Exits], [Expansions], [Literal_ranges], [Spawns]
;              and [Borrows], over the tree pass 5 builds;
; - render/    [To_tree_graph] and [To_span_text].
;
; [Semantics] runs them in order, and [Tst] is the entry module.
(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name tst)
 (libraries cst diagnostic sst source tree_graph))
